        "why_VJTeee": {
          "type": "ow-why",
          "settings": {
            "heading_line1": "There are many reasons to give a damn.",
            "heading_line2": "And we don't need the same reasons.",
            "intro": "Maybe you're here for the vibes and adventure. Or for a damn good cup of coffee. And you don't have to care about the climate for any of that, but there's one thing none of us can opt out of: everything that sustains the fun in this world runs on healthy ecosystems. So drink like you give a damn, whatever your reason (and we will do our part).",
            "col1_title": "Regenerative Farming",
            "col1_body": "Soil health is nurtured by the farmers we grow alongside, season after season, through regenerative agriculture: our direct mechanism for better food and climate resilience.",
            "col2_title": "1% for the Planet",
            "col2_body": "Regenerative farming is just one part of caring for our planet. As members of 1% for the Planet, we give at minimum one percent of annual sales to environmental organisations working hard beyond our own supply chains.",
            "col3_title": "Fully Recyclable",
            "col3_body": "Pretty \"paper\" bags that can't be recycled. BS \"compostable\" claims that don't actually degrade. None of that is eco-friendly. It's plain greenwashing. Ours is fully recyclable: one PE material from start to finish."
          },
          "blocks": {}
